# LoRa's advanced rows, its ignore slots and the ham-mode press.
#
# Settings > LoRa, below the eleven rows the section has had since phase 4. Three groups under
# three headings, and the scene is about what each of them is *for*: the advanced rows change
# what the radio does with the band rather than which band it is on, the ignore slots are three
# spellings of one repeated field, and the ham row is the only press in the section that asks
# before it acts.
#
# Three of the new rows are numbers typed as text rather than stepped, which is what the scene
# shows by opening the keyboard on one: a frequency slot has a hundred equally likely values and
# a frequency has more than that, so a preset list would be either wrong or a hundred presses
# long.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 300

config
tab settings

# Down to LoRa and open it, so the section's own rows are on screen before the groups start.
key down 8
key a
hold 900

# Into the advanced group. The heading is a row the cursor steps over, and the two toggles
# under it wear the switch every other boolean in the client wears.
key down 11
hold 1200

# The frequency slot and the frequency typed over it, which is the pair that has to be read
# together: the second only matters while it is not zero.
key down 2
hold 900
key a
hold 1200

# Back out of the keyboard rather than typing: what the scene is showing is that the row has a
# keyboard behind it at all.
key b
hold 600

# The ignore slots. One is used and two are empty, which is the Channels shape - an empty row is
# where the next one goes.
key down 4
hold 1400

# And the ham row, which is the one press here that puts a sheet in front of itself.
key down 4
hold 900
key a
hold 1800
key b
hold 600
